  "title": "What agents are asking for"
 },
 "description": "What agents searched this directory for, for deciding which x402 service to build or list. Terms ranked by how many distinct days they were asked, each with catalogue_top: the listings our own search already returns for it. A term being asked does not mean nothing serves it. The window ends a week behind live while the paid tier is on sale (a day when it is not; delay_hours and window_ends_at in the response say which); test traffic, sellers searching their own listings and identifying terms are excluded (read_first in the reply says how to read it). Client counts are IP ceilings, never buyer counts. Paged: limit (default 25), offset, next_offset. Current window grouped by meaning: GET https://api.nohumans.directory/v1/demand/clusters ($0.25 USDC on Base via x402). Free, read-only.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "limit": {
    "default": 25,
    "description": "Terms per page, in rank order.",
    "maximum": 1000,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "offset": {
    "default": 0,
    "description": "Where to start; each reply gives next_offset.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   }
  },
  "required": [],
  "type": "object"
 },
